id: pm-dskxwf
title: "PR #935 CI: preserve dependency-free fast-version startup and regenerate runtime contracts"
description: "Exact-head GitHub CI found the new early runtime compatibility wrapper imports PmCliError through the broad SDK runtime-primitives barrel, causing dist-only --version smoke jobs to require fast-json-patch before dependencies are present. The same run found the CLI contract golden fixture stale after new error and command behavior. Restore the dependency-free fast path with the lightweight core error identity and regenerate all owned contract artifacts."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 0
tags[4]: artifact-smoke,ci,contracts,runtime-compatibility
created_at: "2026-08-08T11:29:24.575Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-10T12:05:56.759Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-08T11:39:50.179Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-08T11:39:50.179Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 45
acceptance_criteria: "dependency-free dist --version smoke passes without node_modules; pnpm contracts:check and all generated-surface checks pass; focused tests, exact coverage, and lint remain green"
parent: pm-doxj
severity: high
resolution: "Re-exported the shared error identity from the focused compatibility module, removed the broad runtime barrel from startup, and regenerated the owned CLI contract snapshot."
expected_result: "Dist-only version smoke passes on Node 22/24 and macOS/Ubuntu, and contracts:check is clean on the exact PR head."
actual_result: "The early CLI now imports PmCliError from the focused dependency-light compatibility SDK module, so a copied dist/package artifact runs --version without node_modules. The regenerated contract fixture passes contracts:check; exact coverage and every lint/static gate pass."
component: cli-runtime
